ITEM B50 — Edge-Row Treatment (Row i=0, Latitude 17.50°N)
---------------------------------------------------------
1. Village Count on Edge Row:
   - Exactly 547 villages (3.23% of domain) are assigned to row i=0 (17.50°N).
2. Admissibility & Difference in Treatment:
   - Village-Level Point Downscaling: Edge row is FULLY ADMISSIBLE. The ERA5 atmospheric model runs globally (untruncated grid point), the SRTM DEM at the village centroid is untruncated, and the lapse rate correction Delta T = -Gamma * (z_fine - z_ERA5) is strictly pointwise.
   - Node-Level Orographic Areal Deficit (B47): Edge row is PROBLEMATIC. Evaluating the spatial integral over the 0.25° x 0.25° box [17.375°N, 17.625°N] is truncated at 17.50°N by the northern boundary of the domain mask, resulting in an asymmetric half-box areal average. That is why B47 dropped node (17.50, 74.00).
